---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ControlsGrid from '../../components/ControlsGrid.astro';

const title = 'How to Play Warfare 1942: Controls & Beginner Tips';
const description = 'Learn the published Warfare 1942 browser controls, a fast first-match setup, practical shooter fundamentals, and common loading fixes.';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What is the Wardogs key in Warfare 1942?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'For the published web controls, press U to use the war dog ability. Check the current in-game bindings because another release may differ.'
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/how-to-play/" schema={schema}>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'How to Play', href: '/how-to-play/' }]} />
      <span class="eyebrow">Field manual</span>
      <h1>How to Play Warfare 1942</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede">Load the browser build, confirm your current key bindings, and learn the basic combat loop before committing to a match.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell about-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">60-second start</span>
        <h2>From browser to battlefield</h2>
        <ol class="numbered-list">
          <li>Open the <a href="/unblocked/">browser player</a> and allow the WebGL build to finish loading.</li>
          <li>Use the in-game menu to review sensitivity, audio, quality, and current key bindings.</li>
          <li>Choose the available match or training option shown by your release.</li>
          <li>Move with cover, check the map, and learn the objective before chasing eliminations.</li>
          <li>Use reloads, equipment, and companion abilities when you have space to recover.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <img class="about-grid__image" src="/images/about-battlefield.webp" width="460" height="420" alt="Soldier advancing past a tank in a smoky battlefield" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Direct control answer</span>
      <h2>What is the Wardogs key in Warfare 1942?</h2>
      <p>For the published web controls, press <kbd>U</kbd> to use the war dog ability. “Wardogs key” refers to this keyboard binding, not a promo code or activation key.</p>
      <p>Open the current build's settings before a match to confirm the binding. This guide has not independently documented the Android control layout, and another web release may map the companion ability differently.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Keyboard reference</span>
        <h2>Published web controls</h2>
        <p>Distributor listings currently associate these bindings with the web build. Treat the in-game settings screen as the final authority for the release you load.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Warfare 1942 control differences">
        <table class="version-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Platform</th>
              <th scope="col">Control format</th>
              <th scope="col">Evidence status</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Web browser</th>
              <td>Published keyboard bindings with mouse aiming</td>
              <td>The current published web-control list includes bindings such as <kbd>U</kbd> for the war dog ability, subject to the in-game settings screen for the loaded release.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Android</th>
              <td>Not independently documented</td>
              <td>The Android listing is verified, but its exact on-screen layout and mobile-specific bindings remain unverified. Do not apply the web <kbd>U</kbd> binding to Android.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <ControlsGrid />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell content-grid">
      <article class="content-card"><span class="eyebrow">Position</span><h2>Fight from cover</h2><p>Break sight lines before reloading or changing equipment. Moving through open ground gives several opponents a clean angle at once.</p></article>
      <article class="content-card"><span class="eyebrow">Information</span><h2>Use the map</h2><p>Check the map between fights, not while exposed. Track the objective and nearby routes before choosing the next engagement.</p></article>
      <article class="content-card"><span class="eyebrow">Tempo</span><h2>Reset after contact</h2><p>After a fight, recover, reload, and review equipment before pushing forward. A fast reset is safer than entering the next fight half-ready.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Troubleshooting</span>
      <h2>If Warfare 1942 will not load</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use a current desktop browser with hardware acceleration enabled.</li>
        <li>Disable extensions that block game scripts or third-party frames for this page.</li>
        <li>Close memory-heavy tabs and reload the player.</li>
        <li>Try the external CrazyGames fallback if the embedded frame is blocked.</li>
        <li>Remember that school or workplace networks may block browser games regardless of this site's availability.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>For platform identity and installation safety, continue to the <a href="/download/">download guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
